# Cloudflare Pages cache rules.
#
# This file is the root cause fix for "I deployed, reloaded, and got a blank
# page that survives reloads until I clear site data".
#
# Without it, the browser is free to cache index.html. index.html names the
# hashed bundles for ITS deploy — /assets/index-A1B2C3.js and friends. Deploy
# again and those names change. A reload then serves the CACHED html, which
# asks for chunks that are no longer the current ones, the dynamic import
# rejects, and React renders nothing. Reloading repeats it, because the reload
# is served from the same cache. Clearing site data drops the cached html,
# which is why that appeared to be the only cure.
#
# The rule is simple: the entry document must always be revalidated, and the
# hashed assets it points at can be cached forever because their names change
# whenever their contents do.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Content-hashed by Vite, so a given URL's bytes never change. Safe to keep
# for a year, and this is what keeps repeat visits fast despite the above.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Static files we overwrite in place rather than hashing, so they revalidate.
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/intro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
